      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion.\nIt is the follow-up in change [97000], on top of this change and the docs change [96992]. This change was pushed again only to fix its test, which lists the invalid record before the valid one so that dropping it must not stop the valid one from loading.\n\nIt follows your suggestion except that the tokens are not stored in `EMConfig`. A new `ParsedConfig` holds an `EMConfig` and its tokens, and `ParsedConfig::make` returns `std::nullopt` for an invalid Probe, so the Probe is still parsed once and every instance is valid. A scan copies an `EMConfig` per device and resolves the templates in its statements, so tokens kept there would stop matching them. \n\nThe tokens are held through a `std::shared_ptr\u003cconst\u003e` to avoid copying them on every scan, and I can use a plain `std::vector` if you prefer.\n\nI plan to send the AND/OR placement checks later in their own change.\n\n[97000]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/97000\n[96992]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/96992",
